text:
marta: I'm putting together a tiny migration + examples PR to help teams move from ad-hoc regex parsing to our json_schema structured output. goals: migration checklist, micro SDK examples (py/js), streaming caveats, and two broken-anchor fixes. branch: docs/jsonschema-migration
devon: 👍 include a short decision guidance: when to enforce schema vs allow best-effort parsing. a small table or bullets will help customers decide
hiro: also call out the snake_case vs camelCase key differences between Python and JS SDKs (structured_output vs structuredOutput). we've seen examples mix them and confuse users
kaela: please add a one-liner for handling validation failures: retry once, then fallback to text parser, or return an explicit schema error to the caller. example: `if res.errors: fallback_to_text_parser()`
marta: draft snippets below; keeping them intentionally tiny so they fit into a single docs callout. feel free to quick-nit
```python
# python SDK minimal example: validate tool output with JSON Schema
from redwood import RedwoodClient
c = RedwoodClient()
resp = c.call_tool(
    name="summarize_invoice",
    input={"invoice_text": "..."},
    structured_output={
        "type": "json_schema",
        "schema": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {"total": {"type": "number"}},
            "required": ["total"]
        }
    }
)
# use resp.output (validated) or inspect resp.errors for validation issues
```
```js
// js SDK minimal example: camelCase style
import { RedClient } from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new RedClient();
const res = await client.callTool({
  name: 'summarize_invoice',
  input: { invoice_text: '...' },
  structuredOutput: {
    type: 'json_schema',
    schema: { type: 'object', properties: { total: { type: 'number' } }, required: ['total'] }
  }
});
// res.output is validated JSON; res.errors contains violations
```
hiro: add a short streaming caveat note: when streaming=true partial chunks may not validate. recommend either stream=false for critical validations or use `buffer_full_response=True` to reassemble before validation. link the runtime issue: https://github.com/redwood-inference/runtime/issues/432
devon: also update the two broken links in the docs landing that 404: replace `/docs/tooling/call` -> `/docs/tool-calling/` and `/docs/structured-output/#jsonschema` -> `/docs/structured-output/#json-schema`. call out in the PR description so changelog picks it up
marta: migration checklist (short):
- audit prompts that used regex extraction
- author minimal schema with required fields
- run validation mode=warn for 48h to detect regressions
- after confidence, switch to enforce and open backport PR for stable branch if customers are pinned
kaela: add suggested changelog blurb too so release notes capture it
